{% extends "base.twig" %}

{% block mainContent %}
    <div class="lg:px-4 pb-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl pb-4 text-font-title">Game Development</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
            During my time at the {% include './Components/extLink.twig' with {'link' : "https://games-academy.de/", 'content': 'Games Academy'} %}, I gained first-hand, practical experience in game development.
            I spent the first two of my five semesters at GA as a game design student and the last three as a game programmer.
            Throughout this time, I was able to experience the many facets of game development with curiosity and enthusiasm. Each semester consisted of developing a project within eight weeks.
            All departments represented in the games industry were staffed by students from different departments at GA.
            This allowed us to simulate a practice-oriented small indie studio and experience first-hand how game development works.
            From brainstorming to the conceptualization and design phase, full production, and finally to the gold master.
            We weren't spared the stress of deadlines either, and some would even report occasional crunch times, but that's just nonsense, of course (or is it?).
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
            By the end of my time as a student at GA, I was able to develop up to five semester projects, although the first one was a special exception.
            The first project in the basic semester (the first semester) takes place exclusively within your own course. As a result, the subject areas and departments are not divided efficiently.
            The specifications and technical know-how are also not yet well developed at this stage. This means that the quality differs greatly from the subsequent projects.
            For this reason, it does not feature prominently in the portfolio, but I don't want to withhold it from you either.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
            Possible Mentions:</br>
            - C++ RPG Project</br>
            - C# Game Engine
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="relative card-group flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-4 pt-4">
        {% for project in [
            {
                'link':"https://red-rocket-games.itch.io/crimson-star",
                'extLink':true,
                'tags':["Unity", "Multiplayer", "C#"],
                'time':"2025 — 2025",
                'title':"Crimson Star",
                'description':"The last Project at the Games Academy was a multiplayer, ship building, twin-stick, arena fighter.
                My main tasks were the multiplayer networking code and stability. But as the lead programmer,
                I was involved in task delegation and coordination of four other programmers."
            },
            {
                'link':"https://games-academy.itch.io/kyoto-conflict",
                'extLink':true,
                'tags':["UE5", "Multiplayer", "Blueprint", "C++"],
                'time':"2024 — 2025",
                'title':"Kyoto Conflict",
                'description':"Kyoto Conflict is a fast-paced, first-person shooter, honouring the ancestors of unreal tournament and quake.
                The goal was to achieve a fast and action packed first-person shooter.
                A huge focus put on the movement system enabling bunny hoping and ever accelerating movement.
                Combining fast movement and precise shooting over the network was a big challenge, that I had to overcome.
                In a programming department of just two programmers, this task was enormous but in the end we could present a stable and reliable experience."
            },
            {
                'link':"https://games-academy.itch.io/steambrawl",
                'extLink':true,
                'tags':["UE5", "Multiplayer", "Blueprint"],
                'time':"2024 — 2024",
                'title':"Steambrawl",
                'description':"[[INSERT Steambrawl DESCRIPTION]]"
            },
            {
                'link':"https://games-academy.itch.io/aeternox",
                'extLink':true,
                'tags':["UE5", "UI Development", "Blueprint"],
                'time':"2023 — 2024",
                'title':"Aeternox",
                'description':"[[INSERT Aeternox DESCRIPTION]]"
            },
            {
                'link':"https://games-academy.itch.io/girlz-tankz-n-gunz",
                'extLink':true,
                'tags':["Unity", "Programming", "C#"],
                'time':"2023 — 2023",
                'title':"GirlZ, TankZ 'N GunZ",
                'description':"This is the first project at the Games Academy I was part of. As mentioned earlier, this was the project that was developed in the basic semester.
                I was the only programmer in the team, and relied heavily on my previous experience in own hobbyist projects and my spare time.
                But I was accompanied by very talented artist and a producer, with some prior experience in similar positions.
                Many mistakes were made, but a lot more was learned and very bonding friendship was build, which helped to get settled into the Games Academy."
            },
        ] %}

            {% embed './Components/card.twig' with {'card_link' : project.link, 'ext_link' : project.extLink ,'tags': project.tags, 'card_time': project.time} %}
                {% block cardTitle %}
                    {{ project.title }}
                {% endblock %}
                {% block cardDescription %}
                    {{ project.description }}
                {% endblock %}
            {% endembed %}

        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}